# Security Baseline

## Authentication & authorization

- **JWT** when `AUTH_ENABLED=true`. Library: `python-jose`. Algorithm `HS256` (or `RS256` with managed keys).
- Access token TTL ≤ 60 minutes; **refresh tokens with rotation** (revoke previous on use).
- Authorization via dependency:
  ```python
  Annotated[CurrentUser, Depends(require_scopes("widget.read"))]
  ```
  Never inline `if user.role == "admin":` checks in handlers.
- Admin endpoints require `is_admin=True` **and** a stricter rate limit.

## Password hashing

- `passlib[bcrypt]` with cost factor ≥ **12**.
- Never roll your own KDF.
- `PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12`; reject common passwords (HIBP top-100k list, optional).

## Input

- All bodies via Pydantic with `extra="forbid"`. Reject unknown fields.
- Strip control chars at the edge (utility in `app/utils/text.py`).
- Validate path/query params via `Annotated[..., Field(...)]` constraints.

## Output

- Every route declares `response_model`. Never return raw ORM objects. Map fields explicitly.
- Don't echo back internal IDs unrelated to the requester (IDOR).

## CORS

- `APP_CORS_ORIGINS` is an explicit allowlist. **No wildcard in production.**
- `APP_CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS=true` only when needed.

## Trusted hosts (prod)

- `TrustedHostMiddleware` with `APP_TRUSTED_HOSTS` set to known domains.

## Security headers (middleware)

- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY`
- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`
- `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains` (prod)
- `Content-Security-Policy` — strict on `/docs`; project-tuned otherwise.
- `Permissions-Policy: ()` — deny by default.

## Rate limiting

- Global default via `RATE_LIMIT_DEFAULT` (slowapi, Redis-backed).
- Stricter per-route on auth/sensitive endpoints (`RATE_LIMIT_AUTH`).
- 429 response includes `Retry-After`.

## Secrets

- Env vars only; never logged. Logger redactor masks `*_KEY`, `*_SECRET`, `password`, `token`, `authorization`.
- Use `SecretStr` in settings. Read with `.get_secret_value()` only at the moment of use.
- Rotate on any suspicion of leak. Keep the rotation runbook under `docs/runbooks/` per spec §18.5.

## SQL & mass-assignment

- Parameterized queries only via SQLAlchemy. Raw SQL via `text(...)` with bound params + reviewer comment.
- Pydantic schemas explicitly enumerate writable fields. Never construct ORM objects from raw dicts.

## TLS / transport

- Terminated at Render's load balancer. HTTP→HTTPS redirect; HSTS on.
- Outbound: `httpx` with TLS verification enabled (default). Never `verify=False`.

## Dependency & secret scanning

- `pip-audit` in CI — fail on **High** CVEs.
- `bandit -r app` in CI.
- `detect-secrets` pre-commit + CI.
- Container scan (`trivy` or Render built-in) — fail on **High**.

## Container hardening

- Non-root `app` user. `chown` only what's required.
- Multi-stage build; final stage = minimal runtime, no shell tools, no compilers.
- Read-only root FS where possible (`--read-only` + writable `/tmp` volume).
- Drop Linux capabilities you don't need; `no-new-privileges`.
- Image labels: `org.opencontainers.image.revision`, `version`.

## Audit logging

- Security-sensitive actions (login, role change, admin action, secret rotation) logged via a **dedicated audit logger** with non-redacted user ID + IP. Audit logs are retained longer than app logs and never sampled.

## Data retention & compliance

- PII retention defined per data class. Default: < 90 days unless required.
- Support data export and deletion via service methods (per project, GDPR-style).
- Never cache authenticated user data without per-user keys.

## Hard rules

- ❌ NEVER log raw `Authorization` header or request body containing credentials.
- ❌ NEVER use `eval`, `exec`, or `pickle` on user input.
- ❌ NEVER serve `/docs` publicly in production unless gated.
- ❌ NEVER commit `.env`, `*.pem`, or any secret. `.gitignore` and `detect-secrets` enforce this.

## Review

This rule defines the **baseline controls**; the active review rubric is in `security-review.mdc` — it lists CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW findings with CWE/OWASP references, banned patterns, and §20 escalation triggers. Run the review via `/review-security` (Claude Code) or by referencing `@security-review` in Cursor. Pair with `/review-code` for technical correctness.
